    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d302">

                <pb facs="0525" n="411" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg411"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15a3/1539</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Chargé</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Campbell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-05-07">May 7, 1931</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I venture to send you
                    herewith an <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> on the subject of the
                    difference of opinion between the Italian Government and His Majesty’s
                    Government in the United Kingdom on the one hand and the French Government on
                    the other regarding the interpretation of the “bases of agreement” of March 1st
                    last relative to naval construction. The <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi> contains the considerations my Government instructed me
                    to lay before you. It explains why His Majesty’s Government and the Italian
                    Government consider <pb facs="0526" n="412" xml:id="pg412"/> their
                    interpretation to be correct, and also—which is more important—why neither the
                    French interpretation nor the French proposal of April 20th, (with which you are
                    familiar) could be accepted by His Majesty’s Government.</p>
                <p>It also goes into the reasons why a four year agreement of the kind concerning
                    which the United States Ambassador made enquiries of the First Lord of the
                    Admiralty on May 2nd could not be accepted.</p>
                <p>I hope you may find the <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> useful pending
                    your discussions with Mr. Morrow.</p>
                <p>Meanwhile there are one or two points arising out of the subject matter and our
                    conversation yesterday<anchor n="20" xml:id="d302-f1"/> which I should much like
                    to have an opportunity of discussing with you.</p>
                <p>Believe me [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ronald Campbell</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d302-a1.xml" xpointer="d302-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
